.TH L10N-CONV 1 "February 2026" "l10n-conv 1.0.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
l10n\-conv \- universal localization file converter, validator, and compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B l10n\-conv
[\fIGLOBAL\-OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND\-OPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBl10n\-conv\fR converts between different localization file formats,
validates translation files, compiles them to binary formats, extracts
translatable strings from source code, and shows translation statistics.
.PP
Supported formats include PO (gettext), XLIFF, TS (Qt), JSON, YAML,
ARB (Flutter/Dart), Properties (Java), Strings (Apple), Android XML,
and more.
.PP
Format auto\-detection is used when possible; use \fB\-f\fR/\fB\-\-format\fR
to override.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Output results as JSON for all commands.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output. Only errors are shown.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose output with progress details.
.TP
\fB\-\-about\fR
Show application info (name, version, author, license) and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Show version number and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS convert
Convert between localization file formats.
.PP
.B l10n\-conv convert
\fIINPUT\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.TP
\fIINPUT\fR
Input file path, or \fB\-\fR for stdin.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
Input format. Auto\-detected from file extension if omitted. Required
when reading from stdin.
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format. Required unless \fB\-o\fR specifies a file with a
recognizable extension.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR
Output file. Use \fB\-\fR for stdout.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without writing files.
.TP
\fB\-\-batch\fR
Process all files in a directory recursively.
.PP
Example:
.RS
.nf
l10n\-conv convert messages.po \-\-to xliff \-o messages.xlf
l10n\-conv convert \-f po \-\-to json \-o strings.json < input.po
l10n\-conv convert translations/ \-\-to po \-o output/ \-\-batch
.fi
.RE
.SS compile
Compile localization files to binary formats (.po\[u2192].mo, .ts\[u2192].qm).
.PP
.B l10n\-conv compile
\fIINPUT\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
.TP
\fIINPUT\fR
Input file to compile.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR
Output file path. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without writing.
.PP
Example:
.RS
.nf
l10n\-conv compile po/sv.po \-o locale/sv/LC_MESSAGES/app.mo
.fi
.RE
.SS extract
Extract translatable strings from source code files.
.PP
.B l10n\-conv extract
\fISOURCE_DIR\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.TP
\fISOURCE_DIR\fR
Directory containing source code to scan.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR
Output file for extracted strings. Required.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format. Default: po.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be extracted without writing.
.PP
Example:
.RS
.nf
l10n\-conv extract src/ \-o po/messages.pot
.fi
.RE
.SS check
Validate a localization file for errors and consistency.
.PP
.B l10n\-conv check
\fIFILE\fR [\fB\-f\fR \fIFORMAT\fR]
.TP
\fIFILE\fR
File to validate.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
File format (auto\-detected if omitted).
.PP
Example:
.RS
.nf
l10n\-conv check po/sv.po
l10n\-conv check strings.json \-f json
.fi
.RE
.SS stats
Show translation statistics for a localization file.
.PP
.B l10n\-conv stats
\fIFILE\fR [\fB\-f\fR \fIFORMAT\fR]
.TP
\fIFILE\fR
File to analyze.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
File format (auto\-detected if omitted).
.PP
Shows: total entries, translated, untranslated, fuzzy, completion percentage.
.PP
Example:
.RS
.nf
l10n\-conv stats po/sv.po
  Total: 245, Translated: 230 (93.9%), Fuzzy: 5, Untranslated: 10
.fi
.RE
.SS diff
Compare two localization files and show differences.
.PP
.B l10n\-conv diff
\fIFILE1\fR \fIFILE2\fR [\fB\-f\fR \fIFORMAT\fR]
.TP
\fIFILE1\fR, \fIFILE2\fR
Files to compare.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
File format (auto\-detected if omitted).
.PP
Example:
.RS
.nf
l10n\-conv diff old.po new.po
.fi
.RE
.SS formats
List all supported file formats and their extensions.
.PP
.B l10n\-conv formats
.PP
Example:
.RS
.nf
l10n\-conv formats
  po      .po, .pot       GNU gettext
  xliff   .xlf, .xliff    XLIFF 1.2/2.0
  ts      .ts             Qt Linguist
  json    .json           JSON (i18next, Chrome)
  ...
.fi
.RE
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
PO/POT (GNU gettext), XLIFF 1.2/2.0, TS (Qt Linguist), JSON (i18next,
Chrome extensions), YAML, ARB (Flutter/Dart), Properties (Java),
Strings/Stringsdict (Apple iOS/macOS), Android XML, PHP arrays, CSV.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (conversion completed, file valid, no differences).
.TP
.B 1
Errors found (validation failures, conversion errors, differences found).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown format, file not found, missing required options).
